    "content": "Common (Lonnie Corant Jaman Shuka Rashid Lynn) is an acclaimed American rapper, actor, and author from Chicago, born in 1972. Known for conscious jazz-rap, he won Grammys, an Oscar (2015, \"Glory\"), and an Emmy. Common has starred in films like Selma and John Wick: Chapter 2, and frequently highlights social justice. Key Details About Common: Real Name: Lonnie Rashid Lynn, Jr. Origin: South Side Chicago, IL Early Career: Debuted as \"Common Sense\" with the 1994 album Resurrection. Stage Name Change: Shortened from Common Sense to Common after a lawsuit threat. Musical Style: Conscious rap, jazz-rap, and alternative hip-hop. Notable Relationships: Known for his past relationship with Erykah Badu, whom he collaborated with on the Grammy-winning \"Love of My Life\". Acting Roles: Smokin' Aces, American Gangster, Terminator Salvation, and Just Wright. Activism: Founded the Common Ground Foundation, which focuses on youth education and empowerment. He is a key figure in conscious hip-hop, often collaborating with producers like No I.D. and J Dilla.",
